        "n73-b1-s2"
      ],
      "purpose": "Define the optical-density comparison without confusing it with mass density.",
      "zh": "光密与光疏按本界面上的相对折射率区分；本课研究第一介质折射率高于第二介质的传播方向。",
      "en": "Optically denser and less dense compare the refractive indices at the interface; this lesson considers travel from a higher-index first medium to a lower-index second medium."
    },
    {
      "id": "n73-C02",
      "not_source_quote": true,
      "not_source_erratum": true,
      "status": "pending-independent-SCI-ZHEN",
      "source_sentence_ids": [
        "n73-b2-s6",
        "n73-b5-s1",
        "n73-b6-s2",
        "n73-b6-s3",
        "n73-b6-s5",
        "n73-b6-s6",
        "n73-b6-s7"
      ],
      "purpose": "State the normal-incidence exception and the domain of the sine ratio and strict angle inequalities without replacing any source mathematics.",
      "zh": "两角从界面法线量起。正弦比要求分母非零，正入射时应使用不作除法的折射定律；折射角严格大于入射角的推理限于非零入射角及仍有传播的折射光的范围。",
      "en": "Both angles are measured from the interface normal. The sine ratio requires a nonzero denominator, so normal incidence uses the refraction law without division. The strict refraction-angle inequality applies to nonzero incidence while a propagating refracted ray exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "n73-C03",
      "not_source_quote": true,
      "not_source_erratum": true,
      "status": "pending-independent-SCI-ZHEN",
      "source_sentence_ids": [
        "n73-b7-s1",
        "n73-b7-s3",
        "n73-b7-s5"
      ],
      "purpose": "Keep the observed beam-strength trend and the source percentage while stating an ideal, lossless-interface limit.",
      "zh": "亮度变化作为本实验接近临界条件的观察描述，不把目测亮度直接等同于光能测量，也不主张所有偏振状态和所有入射角区间都有相同的单调变化。反射比例接近百分之百以及全部反射回去按透明、无吸收界面的理想模型理解。",
      "en": "The brightness trend describes this experiment near the critical condition; visual brightness is not equated with an energy measurement, and the same monotonic trend is not claimed for every polarization and incidence-angle interval. A reflected fraction approaching one hundred percent and complete return of the light energy refer to the ideal transparent, nonabsorbing-interface model."
    },
    {
      "id": "n73-C04",
      "not_source_quote": true,
      "not_source_erratum": true,
      "status": "pending-independent-SCI-ZHEN",
      "source_sentence_ids": [
        "n73-b7-s4",
        "n73-b7-s5",
        "n73-b10-s1"
      ],
      "purpose": "Map the source's inclusive critical-angle wording explicitly and distinguish equality from strict-greater incidence without an unconfirmed source erratum.",
      "zh": "原源快照的大于或等于原样保留，现代正文明确说明这是原文的条件表述。等于临界角是沿界面的掠射边界；严格大于临界角时没有向第二介质传播的折射光束。这里的无传播光束不是声称界面另一侧不存在任何电磁场。",
      "en": "The original greater-than-or-equal wording remains unchanged in the source snapshot and is explicitly attributed in the modern prose. Equality is the grazing boundary along the interface; strictly greater incidence gives no refracted beam propagating into the second medium. Absence of a propagating beam does not assert the absence of every electromagnetic field on the other side."
    },
    {
      "id": "n73-C05",
      "not_source_quote": true,
      "not_source_erratum": true,
      "status": "pending-independent-SCI-ZHEN",
      "source_sentence_ids": [
        "n73-b10-s4",
        "n73-b10-s5",
        "n73-b10-s6"
      ],
      "purpose": "Retain all original rounded refractive-index and critical-angle examples without recomputation or precision inflation.",
      "zh": "水、玻璃、金刚石的折射率与角度按原书近似例值保留，三例第二介质均为空气；不由已舍入折射率重新计算并替换原角度，不把材料折射率当作无条件的精确常数。",
      "en": "Retain the source's approximate indices and angles for water, glass, and diamond, with air as the second medium in all three examples. Do not replace the source angles by recalculating from rounded indices, or treat the material indices as unconditional exact constants."
    },
    {
      "id": "n73-C06",
      "not_source_quote": true,
      "not_source_erratum": true,
      "status": "pending-independent-SCI-ZHEN",
      "source_sentence_ids": [
        "n73-b15-s2",
        "n73-b15-s3"
      ],
      "purpose": "Describe the usual core/cladding implementation and qualify the source's any-path wording.",
      "zh": "通常的玻璃光纤以高折射率芯和低折射率透明包层形成导光界面；沿直线或曲线传播仍受入射角和弯曲条件限制，任意急弯不是原理所保证的适用范围。这是现代解释，不冒充原源对各根纤维结构的逐字描述。",
      "en": "A usual glass fiber guides light with a higher-index core and lower-index transparent cladding. Straight and curved propagation remain subject to incidence-angle and bend conditions; arbitrary sharp bends are not guaranteed. This is a modern explanation, not a claim that the source described each fiber's structure in these exact words."
    },
    {
      "id": "n73-C07",
      "not_source_quote": true,
      "not_source_erratum": true,
      "status": "pending-independent-SCI-ZHEN",
      "source_sentence_ids": [
        "n73-b15-s5",
        "n73-b15-s6"
      ],
      "purpose": "State the positional correspondence needed for direct image transport and locate the unwanted bulb heating.",
      "zh": "按原文每根纤维传递像元的说明，直接重现图像还需要输入、输出两端的纤维排列相对应。医学用途保留为内部器官的观察和检查；避免的是把灯泡置于观察部位造成的额外局部发热，不主张光导装置在任何条件下都不产生热。",
      "en": "For direct image reconstruction from the source's individual-fiber image elements, the fiber arrangement must correspond at the input and output ends. The medical use remains observation and examination of internal organs; the avoided heat is extra local heating from a bulb at the observation site, not a claim that a light guide never produces heat."
    }
  ],
